A||||17||TI_3VOM||Fiero-Friendly Shops....||||5||
Z||000000||TI_3VOM||10-29-2001||06:11 PM||||After reading posts on repair/parts/muffler shops that seem to snicker at our cars, even when we want to spend cash on them at THEIR establishment, I was wondering why don't we, as a group, post the names of the shops that seem to actually enjoy working on our little beauties? No, I'm not talking about the Fiero specific businesses that cater to our niche, but a kind of "where to go" of the local independents that takes on all comers and treats each car and owner with respect and a professional attitude. Conversely, how about an "avoid at all costs" list of the shops/people that just want to rip us off? TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||Philphine||10-29-2001||09:43 PM||||i don't know about enjoyment but they do realy good work and it's the only shop where i don't feel like they're going to take advantage of me if they get the chance. a shop called hunt and knight in jeffersontown, ky. (big suburb city of louisville). not a gm dealer but they only work on gm cars, and specialize in vettes. if you go by there's always a few parked out front, but they don't seem to mind working on my fiero when i need serious work done. haven't been there in a few years but meet one of the main guys recently and he remembered me. great shop.||||reg||1
Z||000002||recluse||10-29-2001||11:11 PM||||I dont know, I've never taken any of my Fieros to a shop.||||reg||6
Z||000003||fiero56||10-29-2001||11:13 PM||||Jack Walker Pontiac in Centerville is the only place I will allow to touch my Fieros. I've only had them perform service for me twice, but both times I was very impressed by the work and courtesy/service I received. <P>Plus, they always seem confident about working on a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DR650SE||10-29-2001||11:38 PM||||This is a good idea. Usually I got to Jay Pontiac in Bedford Hts. Ohio.  Its in north eastern ohio where the Cleveladn Fieros club meets.  They did work for me once and it was good service.  Usually I do my own work though.  That was the only time i took it to a shope cuz i was stupmed.  Clutch wouldn't disengage(prob that I'm having now again)  turned out it was a bent clutch fork.  I may do it my self this time.  Anyone know of anyother places in NE Ohio?  I would like to know of for future referance.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||10-30-2001||04:42 AM||||I think this has been covered before, but here's my vote anyway.<P>Dorais Chevrolet in Wabash, IN.  Hands down the friendliest folks in any shop within 100 miles.  Good prices, very competent, etc.  Just ask for Tim or Karla and tell them I sent ya!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Flamberge||10-30-2001||05:03 AM||||I went to a place in Denver after having my fuel pump go out, and the guy was not very familiar with Fieros...at all.... &gt; <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> In fact, I talked to him and he said "So the Fiero...is that..uh...the one where the engine is in the back?" *sigh* I should have taken it somewhere else, but I was already strapped for time, and there wasn't any other cars he had to work on. (Gee I wonder why.) Anyway, at least it was my Red Fiero (the one I don't have any more) and not this one.<P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||onfire||10-30-2001||05:50 AM||||My friend owns his own shop I take it there. He doesn't seem to mind working on my Fiero. Of course we haven't got to the big brake project yet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>C & S Automotive<BR>Seatac, WA <P>Burien Firestone <BR>My uncle works there.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||10-30-2001||08:20 AM||||O'Hare Pontiac on River Road and Oakton in Des Plaines, IL is a "Fiero Friendly" dealer. They even have 2 guys who are qualified/certified to work on Fiero's.<BR>Ask for Bob P. (service advisor) to schedule a repair.<P>I also have a list of "Fiero Friendly" places that I was put out by NIFE for all it's members. There are over 100 recommended businesses in the Chicagoland area. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000009||JohnF||10-30-2001||08:58 AM||||In the Dallas/Ft. Worth metromess, H & K Automotive in North Richland Hills has a Fiero mechanic as a co-owner. Treats every Fiero as a show car!  Reasonable and quick.  <P>They even allow you to supply parts for them to install and pass thru only the exact costs of any parts they provide.||||reg||10
Z||000010||stimpy||10-30-2001||09:31 AM||||Of course, a big shout out goes to Big O Tires on Prescott Road in Modesto CA, (Hi dad.) Alignments a specialty.<P>I always take my car to Precision Tune-Up center on Western south of SW 74th street here in OKC. Very reasonable rates, will let me bring in my own new parts, and get the work done quickliy and right.<P>And WalMart for Mobil 1 oil changes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Oh, one more. In Central California, go to Tracy Muffler in Tracy. (No muff too tuff is there motto.) Family-owned business, good people, good prices, great service. Worth the drive from anywhere in the Bay Area. Plus there is a Dairy Queen next door while you wait...<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||crash||10-30-2001||09:34 AM||||I met the best guy ever when I got in a fiero related accident. His wife drove by in her fiero and stopped and gave me his no. And told me that they could help me. <BR>He is an awesome guy. I have built stuff with him and I am going nowhere else with my work.<BR>He is a private party so I will ask him If he is ok with divulging his info, but If anyone ever breaks down in the surrounding area of Grand Rapids, MI give me a call @ 616 4555623 and we'll come help you out.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||DXR_DAD||10-30-2001||10:26 AM||||Yes MM we did this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So the the new members<BR>If your in the Bay Area, South San Francisco go to: <BR>Taylormade Automotive<BR>1361 San Mateo Ave.<BR>South San Francisco, Ca<BR>650/873-2022<P>Ask for Chris Gibbs he's the owner and a very good guy to deal with! They will work on anything. They do lots of custom cars, Hot Rods, Classics, <BR>PS. look at the wall of fame if you go by<BR>ASE Master Machanic, GM Certs, and a lot of others.<P>Miguel is the service manager you can also speak to him.<P><BR>DXR_DAD ||||reg||14
Z||000013||Raydar||10-30-2001||12:39 PM||||Lou Sobh Buick/Pontiac/Olds on Thornton Rd.  Just west of Atlanta. Ask for David in the parts dept. <BR>Also Custom Mufflers on Bankhead Highway near Lithia Springs. Does a lot of performance stuff. <BR>Wasn't afraid to mess with a Fiero. Even said he could order me a Borla system. This was about three years ago. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000014||trigger||10-30-2001||01:22 PM||||I have two shops where I'll take my car.  The first is where I work<P>Deutmeyer Auto Advantage<BR>Dyersville, Iowa 52040<BR>1-(563)-875-7993<P>The other guy has weird hours but really good prices.  If you stop tell him Anthony Wright sent you.<P>Weber Enterprises<BR>Ryan, Iowa<BR>1-(563)-932-2128<P>Otherwise if you break down near Dyersville, or are just in the area stop by, I have tools and a decent sized garage.<P>704 5th Ave. S.E.<BR>Dyersville, IA 52040<BR>1-(563)-875-2170<P>ask for Anthony<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||10-30-2001||02:23 PM||||Engineered Performance is Fiero Tolerant. they've messaged my SE my GT, Donalds Turbo, Black GTs GT, and 3 V8 swap cars... 2 4cyls.. well i end up doing some of the work but thats ok...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>oh yeah..  north Atlanta...  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||thomas_l||10-30-2001||04:21 PM||||Mighty Muffler in Duluth, GA did my catalytic convertor. Not exactly what I'd call a sanitary shop, but they didn't squeak about the Fiero or get stupid with pricing. They did a prompt re-check on a rattle and fixed it. Then a few weeks later tacked on another hanger on the back (first side replaced on the first trip) for $10, no wait.<P>After I get through with my other dozen projects (especially the ones that have cash value  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) I will probably get them to run dual exhaust on my 02 Silverado since they passed the Fiero test.<P>For mechanicals, I am my own favorite. ASE certs (ok they were valid when my Fiero was built) and I give myself a great labor rate. Nice clean garage, convenient to home. Wait, it IS my home.<P>Jury's still out on paint. I haven't gotten the nerve to do my own yet and the one car I had done locally doesn't warrant a recommendation. One of the above mentioned projects is a 94 Crown Vic police car that will probably be the one that buys the home spray gear  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||Heretic||10-30-2001||06:40 PM||||I dont own a Fiero , BUT i know a place called Evans Racing Proucts here in Cambridge. I've heard they do excellent work. One of the mechanics there owns a NICE GT , not sure of the year, so that is always a plus.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://shopping.yimg.com/images/muze/album/390/399801_th.jpg">    <BR>TOOL OWNS j00!||||reg||1
